# Beszel agent environment template.
#
# Installed by deploy/provision.sh to /etc/jiuyue/beszel.env (mode 0640,
# root:root) and loaded by beszel-agent.service via EnvironmentFile=.
#
# NEVER commit a filled-in copy: the key/token are credentials. This template
# carries placeholders only.

# --- hub -> agent (default) --------------------------------------------------
# The hub generates a key pair when you add a system in its UI ("Add system"
# -> copy the public key). Paste that PUBLIC key here; the agent uses it to
# authorize the hub. The hub then connects to LISTEN.
KEY=REPLACE_WITH_AGENT_PUBLIC_KEY
# Keep the agent on loopback; the hub reaches it locally (or over an SSH tunnel).
LISTEN=127.0.0.1:45876

# --- agent -> hub (edge mode, optional) --------------------------------------
# Alternatively the agent can dial OUT to the hub using a token from the UI.
# Set HUB_URL and TOKEN instead of KEY when the hub cannot reach the agent.
# HUB_URL=https://beszel.example.com
# TOKEN=REPLACE_WITH_AGENT_TOKEN
